<title>USA: Wall Street technology shares hit by Intel at opening.</title>
<headline>Wall Street technology shares hit by Intel at opening.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK</dateline>
<text>
<p>The stocks of technology companies fell sharply in early trading Friday, hit by bellwether Intel Corp.'s warning that its second-quarter results would be below expectations.</p>
<p>The Dow Jones industrial average lost 45 points to 7,285 in the first seven minutes of trading. Intel plummeted $20.77 to $143 on Nasdaq, with 4.7 million shares traded.</p>
